  "raw_text": "301\n\nNegative - Future / Negativa - Futuro\n\nThe\n \n“\nNegative\n \n–\n \nFuture\n”\n \nform\n \nis formed by adding “ra” to the end of a verb conjugated in the Future II tense\n.\n\n1\nst\n \nperson: Root + amna + ra;\n \n2\nnd\n \nperson: Root + ma + ra; 3\nrd\n \nperson: Root + bia + ra\n\nIt can be used in a prohibitive way also (a\n \nmore gentle prohibitive form)\n \n–\n \nsomething that is not to be done.\n\nLa forma “Negativa\n \n–\n \nFuturo” se forma agregando \"ra\" al final de un verbo conjugado en el tiempo Futuro II.\n\n1\ner\n \npersona: Raíz + amna + ra;\n \n2\ndo\n \npersona: Raíz + ma + ra; 3\ner\n \npersona: Raíz + bia + ra\n\nTambién se puede utilizar de forma prohibitiva (una forma prohibitiva más suave)\n \n–\n \nalgo que no hacer.\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nDawanki, ninam sin lahtubi\n \naisamnara sîa\n \n(\ndb\n-\nSins Laka 30:9\n)\n \n–\n \nout of fear\n,\n \nso as not to curse your name my Lord\n \n/\n\npor miedo\n,\n \npara no maldecir tu nombre mi Señor\n\nMan sin witin wal baku kra takmara sîa\n \n(\ndb-Sins Laka 26:4\n)\n \n–\n \nout of fear, so as not to become like him\n \n/ por miedo,\npara no volverse como él\n\nNaha tasba na yawan latwan kaikbiara\n \n–\n \nWe are not to love this world\n \n/ No debemos amar este mundo\n\nLalah briaia ba diara tara sa\n.\n \nSakuna maritkam lâka ra yarka saura munbiara.\n \n–\n \nIt is important to have money.\n\nHowever, we are not to allow it to harm your marriage.\n \n/ Es importante tener dinero.\n \nSin embargo, no debemos\npermitirle dañar tu matrimonio.\n\nNegative / Negativa\n\nThe negative form is usually formed by adding\n \n“\nras\n”\n \nto the root of the verb /\n\nLa forma negativa generalmente se forma agregando \"\nras\n\" a la raíz del verbo\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nB\nî\nla walaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto obey, to listen to the word of\n \n/ obedecer, escuchar la\n \npalabra de\n\n→\n \nAdam ba\n \nbîla walras kan minitka ra Jehova aihni pali dîa dau\nkan?\n \n–\n \nWhat did Jehovah do immediately at the\n\nminute Adam disobeyed?\n \n/ Qué hizo Jehová inmediatamente en el momento en que Adán desobedeció?\n\nPaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto create\n \n/ crear\n\n→\n \ntasba na diara\n \nâ\npu kaia dukiara paskras kan\n \n–\n \nthis earth was not created for nothing\n \n/\n \nesta tierra no fue creada\n\npara nada\n\nConditional\n\nThere is a form of the verb where “\nai\n” is added to the root of the verb t\no make it conditional.\n \nI\nt is often heard\n \nin\n\nconversation.\n\nHay una\n \nforma del verbo donde se agrega \"\nai\n\" a la raíz del verbo para hacerlo\n \nconditional\n.\n \nA\n \nmenudo se escucha en\n\nla conversación.\n\nExamples/Ejemplos:\n\nW\naitna kum nina Manoa m\nâ\nki kan ba, witin aisa kum takai ba nu takan taim\n, …\n \n–\n \nThe man called Manoah, when he\n\ncame to know that he would be a father, …\n \n/ El hombre llamó a Man\nó\nah, cuando se enteró de que sería un padre, ...\n\n(\nfy63\n)\n\nJu nani mita naha waitnika na alki ikai kan\n \n–\n \nThe Jews were about to kill this man\n \n/ Los judíos estaban a punto de\n\nmatar a este hombre\n \n(\ndb\n-\nApastil Nani\n \nSturka\n \n23:27\n)\n\nMeri waitnika kum nina Josep wal marit takai kan\n \n–\n \nMary was to be married to a man named Joseph\n \n/ María debía\ncasarse con un hombre llamado José\n \n(\nlfb69\n)\n\nJehova sain kum yan witin ra hilp munai ba marikaia dukiara\n \n–\n \nJehovah gave a sign in order to show that he would\nhelp him\n \n/ Jehová dio una señal para demostrar que lo ayudaría\n \n(\nlfb18\n)\n\nFor\n \nmore examples, see: / Para más ejemplos, ver:\n\nMunai\n \n(\nbh87,lfb18\n);\n \nLukai\n \n(\nlv181\n);\n \nDaukai\n \n(\nmy59\n);\n \nWai\n \n(\nmy80,my113,dbta\n-\nImpakan Sturka\n \n12:28,dbta\n-\nKulki Kaikanka\n\n12:16,dbta\n-\n2\n \nKing\n \nNani\n \n2:3,5\n);\n \nIwai\n \n(\nlv110,my3,my55\n);\n \nBalai\n \n(\nbh194,bh197,bh198\n,\ngf12\n);\n \nKai\n \n(\nbh177\n,\ndbta\n-\nKli Smalkanka\n\n8:17\n,\ndbta\n-\nWihta Nani\n \n21:17\n);\n \nBlikai\n \n(\nbh39\n);\n \nIkai\n \n(\nbh205\n,\nmy14\n,\nmy29\n,\ndb\n-\nA\npastil Nani Sturka\n \n23:2\n7\n);\n \nTakai\n \n(\nbh86\n,\nbh108\n,\nbh182\n,\n\nbh217\n,\nfy63\n,\n \nlv50\n,\nlv110\n,\nlv116\n,\nlv153\n,\n \nlv183\n,\n \nkm10/15\n,\nmy50\n,\nmy65\n,\nmy84\n,\nsny109\n,\ndba\n-\n2\n \nT\nesalonika\n-\nintro\n,\ndbta\n-\nLawana Nani\n \n45\n-\n\nintro\n,\ndbta\n-\nAiseya\n \n49note\n/nota\n);\n \nSakai\n \n(\nmy101\n)",
